-- lib/intproof.cub — integers as differences of words (lib/std.cub's Z2, toZ2, fromZ2, addZ, leZ):
-- the commutative-monoid laws of addZ through the coordinates, and the linear-arithmetic
-- certificate checker over Int, verified by reduction to lib/linproof.cub's over words (
-- PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F32): an Int linear form is a pair of word forms over doubled variables (variable v's
-- coordinates are the word variables 2v and 2v + 1), a ≤ b over Int is a⁺ + b⁻ ≤ b⁺ + a⁻ over
-- words, and a Farkas certificate of the word problem is one of the Int problem (int-cert-sound).
-- Loaded after lib/linproof.cub.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the monoid laws
-- the commutative monoid, through the coordinates
cong2Z : (f : Z2 → Int) → {a b c d : Word} → a ≡ b → c ≡ d → f (a , c) ≡ f (b , d)
cong2Z f p q = λ i → f (p i , q i)
